WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.580
May 30

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:08.650
Girls, make sure you all 
bring your lunches tomorrow.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:09.900
Lunches?

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.560
For tomorrow's happiness training, 
we'll spend the day

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.870
on a nearby mountain for some 
"good luck orienteering."

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.200
Good luck...

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.830
Orienteering?

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.830
Make sure you follow me, okay?

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:33.320
Field trip, field trip!

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:35.930
Thank you.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.720
Let's see...

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.300
What else?

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.980
Good luck orienteering, huh?

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.080
Anyway, I think I might've 
bought too much for lunch.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.010
Timo, Timo, Timo, Timo...

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.500
Timo, Timo, Timo, Timo...

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.560
Timo, Timo, Timo, Timo, Timo!

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.860
There are several power spots 
scattered around the mountain.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.770
Power spots?

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.270
Today you'll visit each of these 
checkpoints to gather good luck.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.540
Good luck, huh?

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.030
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.030
<b>May 30</b>

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.030
<b>A Field Trip With Everyone</b>

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:06.160
Leading all of you unfortunate girls 
is too difficult a task for me alone,

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.370
so I've asked for some help.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.990
Hey. It's me, Timothy.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:16.050
Today I've come dressed as 
my golden good luck version.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.300
Wow! It's a sparkly Timothy!

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.420
Why does he look so cheap 
even though he's gold?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.220
I'm three times faster than normal.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.460
Timothy, if you move around 
too much, your disguise—

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.560
I mean, the gold will come off.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:38.280
Then let's draw lots now to 
determine your starting order.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.280
Lottery

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.240
Me! I'll do it!

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.240
<b>Last</b>

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.260
It's the real deal...

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.380
You three have such terrible luck,
I'm not even counting you.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:48.950
We're the last team to start.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:50.840
Later.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.480
I can't say I didn't expect it,
but we really are last.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.660
Sorry.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.590
Don't worry about it.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.940
All right, last team, I'll follow along behind you

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:04.470
and be your guardian angel.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:07.180
I have a bad feeling about this...

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.800
<i>I really came to laugh at you.</i>

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.630
It's so warm!

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.460
Yeah.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.640
It feels nice.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.110
Please wait...

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.110
Please...

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:26.410
Please wait, you two...

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.830
Are you okay?

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.830
Current location: lost.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.420
I'm not very good at climbing hills.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.580
I'm sorry for making you carry my bag.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.300
I don't mind, but are you sure you're okay?

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.760
I'd rather force myself to 
participate and die than miss out

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.220
on such a beautiful opportunity
to make memories with you!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.760
Yeah, don't push yourself, okay?

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.980
Wow, how cute!

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.230
There are kitties out here, too!

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.350
Black cats... And a whole group of them?

00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.740
My shoelaces!

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.360
How did both of them suddenly break?

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.610
Shoelaces?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:06.040
I thought this might happen, 
so I brought spares...

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.990
My favorite bowl is split in two!

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:14.500
<b>Rustle Rustle</b>

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.250
And this... And this...

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.500
And this, and this, and this...

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.500
They're too unlucky.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.920
Will this really improve our luck?

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.630
Hibari-chan.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.040
Do you know what that is?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.720
It's the song of a <i>hibari</i> (skylark).

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.740
I'm so happy to hear it in person like this!

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:43.120
Well, luck aside, as long as we're doing this,

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.530
let's try to enjoy ourselves.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:46.030
You're right.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:46.820
Yeah!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.370
Hey, a bridge!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.500
Hanako-san!

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:52.080
Hanako!

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.080
Hanako!

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.210
It's my time to shine!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:05:59.210
<b>Konk</b>

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.170
So this is what it is to be young...

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.340
Hanako, are you okay?

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.340
<b>Float
Float</b>

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.340
<b>Drag</b>

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.700
A great escape...

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.160
That was a close call.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.860
Y-You and bridges really don't get along!

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:15.560
Really?

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.520
Here.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:20.200
It won't be dangerous if we're holding hands.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.520
Let's go.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.980
Yeah!

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.250
What a heartwarming sight.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.780
Botan-chan, take this side.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.170
Okay.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:37.530
Hibari-chan, you worry too much.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.820
Only because it's you.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.290
Hey!

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.870
Don't stop us from crossing by holding hands!

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.930
Oh, Hibiki-chan and Ren-chan!

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:46.590
Hey.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:48.750
How are you behind us?

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:49.980
Shut up!

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.920
Hey, hey! Why don't you come with—

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:52.950
I refuse!

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:54.510
What?

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:55.970
<b>Scritch</b>

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:55.970
<b>Scritch</b>

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.940
Monkeys?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:04.720
Wow, that monkey is using a knife!

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.510
How dexterous.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:09.620
It must have picked up one
that somebody dropped.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:14.650
Since they're not reacting to Ren,
they must not be female.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.390
This isn't the time to discuss it!

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:18.620
Let's run!

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:27.240
Hey! No fair!

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:36.970
What the heck was that?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.850
Hey!

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.570
You're the last ones.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:45.320
Did you run into any misfortune?

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.930
No, we had tons of fun!

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:49.940
We only got caught up in theirs!

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:56.160
The first good luck checkpoint 
is just beyond this hill.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.470
It's beautiful!

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:04.880
Let's eat lunch here to gather more luck.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.210
Sheet flip!

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:07.880
Hey, wait!

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.580
This place is so pretty.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.680
I've always wanted to climb this mountain.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:15.980
Huh?

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:17.300
What's wrong?

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.770
My lunch is gone.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.190
I know I put it in my bag...

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.600
Did you drop it somewhere?

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.640
Tasty, tasty!

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:28.000
Rolled omelets!

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:28.610
Tasty!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.940
<b>Stagger...</b>

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.940
Hanako-san, where are you going?

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:33.640
I'm going to find some edible grasses.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.530
<b>Gloom</b>

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:34.530
Don't!

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.030
That's poisonous!

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.530
So are those mushrooms!

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.410
You know a lot about plants, Hibari-san.

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:43.900
I learned a lot about them
through my parents' work.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.130
Don't eat any more grass.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:48.650
Here.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.180
Let's eat together.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.440
You can have some of my lunch, too.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:56.050
Thanks, guys.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:58.630
Let's eat!

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:03.520
Hibiki-chan and Ren-chan!

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:06.140
Would you like to join us?

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:08.460
Why do we have to eat here with—

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:09.050
Yeah.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.240
How dare you seduce Ren with food?

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:15.500
Ren.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:17.610
You can eat this.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.080
They're my special sandwiches.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:25.580
I'm sure you guys want some, 
but I won't let you have a single—

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:32.670
They taste a little weird
after all that running earlier.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.010
Do you want to eat with us?

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:39.620
Here.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.680
I'll allow myself to fall for your tricks.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.440
Then let's start over again.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.100
Yeah.

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.320
Let's eat!

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.860
I could keep going.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.700
Th-These fried shrimp taste like shrimp!

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.580
What? There are fried shrimp that don't?

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:08.540
My mom turns all her fried food into charcoal.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:09.910
Charcoal?

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:13.530
They're too good!

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:16.550
What a cute and tasty-looking lunch.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.430
I made a little too much today.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.930
You made all this, Hibari-san?

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:27.560
Yeah. My parents are always working overseas,

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.940
so I have to cook for myself.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:32.620
What? Does that mean you live alone?

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:34.560
Yeah, but just so you know,

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.510
that doesn't mean I'm lonely or anything.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:37.320
You're lucky!

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:42.320
That means your mom and dad really trust you!

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.330
That's not...

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.690
After all, you can make 
delicious lunches like this.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.620
It's good.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.020
Yeah, it is.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:02.240
And today it tastes extra good 
because we're eating it together.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:03.640
You're right.

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:06.440
Together...

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:11.750
<i>I see.</i>

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:18.890
<i>Maybe that's what this
happiness training is all about.</i>

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:24.410
Girls, this field of flowers 
doesn't have much luck,

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.260
so once you've finished eating, 
let's move on to the next place.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:28.580
It doesn't?

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.780
Repainting.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:35.460
After meals is this one and this one...

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:39.670
I'm going to wash the spoon and fork
I borrowed from Hibari-chan.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:40.880
What?

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.810
Wash them?

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:43.840
Botan-chan, wait right there!

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:43.840
Hanako-san?

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:46.850
I'm back.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:49.310
I'm leading the group this time!

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:52.280
Here I go!

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.200
Our next checkpoint is a waterfall

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:54.860
that will immerse you in good luck.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.870
We should start getting ready, too.

00:11:57.430 --> 00:11:59.820
Huh? Where's Hanako?

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.990
She said she was going to wash
the spoon she borrowed...

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:05.720
Could it be...

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:08.430
Hanako!

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:10.350
Hanako-san!

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:16.240
Hibari-san, did you find her?

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:18.180
No, she's not here.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.740
This is Hanako's!

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:26.490
Hanako!

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:35.070
What shall we do?

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:38.980
If only I'd stopped Hanako-san...

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.050
I've always been like this.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.300
Because of the weak constitution 
I got from my mother,

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:47.570
just worrying about myself 
takes all of my energy.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:50.440
We're supposed to be good luck orienteering,

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:52.440
but I'm slow, stupid, and clueless.

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:56.540
It's my fault for insisting on coming 
when I'm a failure of a human being.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:01.510
Oh, just thinking Hanako-san could be 
experiencing some misfortune somewhere...

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.860
Listen, we don't know that 
anything has happened to her yet.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.470
But we're talking about Hanako-san here.

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:16.450
Uh, but...

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:17.440
Remember,

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.480
<b>Good Luck</b>

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.400
Hanako basically has the devil's luck.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.480
<b>Great Luck</b>

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:20.480
<b>Financial Luck</b>

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.480
<b>Better Luck</b>

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.940
The devil's luck?

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.940
<b>Devil's Luck</b>

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:25.070
So I'm sure she's fine.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:26.700
Let's hurry up and find her, okay?

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:30.330
You might be right.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:34.600
Fine. If you insist, we'll help you look for her.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:35.540
When did you get here?

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:37.840
We're already involved, anyway.

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:39.400
Let's go, Ren.

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:42.250
We'll look for her downstream.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:46.820
Teacher!

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.350
What's wrong?

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:53.580
Hanako is... I mean, 
Hanakoizumi-san has gone missing.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.560
Hanakoizumi-san?

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.590
She's been missing since she
said she was going to wash

00:13:58.590 --> 00:13:59.980
her utensils after lunch.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:03.370
I understand. I'll send Timothy to find her.

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:05.200
Timothy, did you hear that?

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:08.680
<i>Roger. I'll go look for her immediately.</i>

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.950
You should try searching around the area, too.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.520
Okay. Let's go.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:13.290
Okay.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.660
<i>Her bad luck shouldn't be taken lightly.</i>

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:22.840
Calling CQ. Come in, CQ.

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:26.840
This is Kilo, India, Romeo, Romeo...

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:31.100
<i>I have an unprecedentedly 
strange feeling about this.</i>

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:34.150
Could it be...

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.370
That's all for today.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.770
I can't believe she's missing.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:43.200
What a troublesome girl.

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.990
Hibiki, not that way.

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:47.850
I-I know where I'm going.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.410
<b>We apologize for the inconvenience.</b>

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.060
What's wrong?

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.250
Nothing. Let's go, Ren.

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:03.790
I can fly.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.250
No!

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.300
Hanako!

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.330
Hanako-san!

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.370
She doesn't seem to be here, either.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.680
Let's try checking downstream, too.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:16.660
Okay.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:18.860
Hanako!

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:20.650
Hanako-san!

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.060
Hanako!

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:24.800
Hanako-san!

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.100
Hanako!

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:28.490
That's...

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:31.450
Huh? Hibari-san?

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:36.040
What is... What is he doing here?

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:39.290
That's...

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:41.540
Your boyfriend.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.920
B-B-B-Boyfriend?!

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.940
N-No, no! Not yet!

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.380
Huh? "Yet"?

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.970
Forget it! Let's go!

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:57.660
Wait! Look where his arrow is pointing!

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:02.560
Hanako!

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.560
Hanako-san, get a hold of yourself.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.000
What were you doing here?

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:11.900
Well, at first, while I was washing 
your utensils in the creek,

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:15.780
I noticed my hairpin was missing.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.540
<b>Splish Splash</b>

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.540
<b>Splooosh</b>

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:19.640
Then I fell in the river looking for it.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:24.540
<b>Clatter
Clatter</b>

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:21.800
I couldn't find anything to grab,

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:24.710
so I got washed downstream
as rocks fell on me.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.580
I got attacked by fish, too.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:32.550
For some reason, the monkeys
smiled and waved at me, though.

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:36.060
Then, finally, I was able to crawl out here.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:37.620
That's even worse than I thought.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:40.060
Oh, you found her.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:41.730
You sure do cause a lot of trouble.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:44.020
Sorry.

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.400
Hibiki, you kept getting lost, too.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.110
Th-That's...

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:51.550
This is a tonic. Here.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:53.240
I wasn't lost. I was just trying to, uh...

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:53.240
Thanks, Botan-chan!

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:56.280
It may be a little sour.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.380
How do I open this?

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:00.940
You twist this to the right...

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:02.620
Oh, I got it! Thanks!

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:04.820
What's wrong, Hibiki?

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:07.710
It's nothing.

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:15.080
Let's go back and tell the teacher
that we're dropping out.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.770
What? We'll be okay.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.550
I'm all warmed up now.

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:22.840
That's just Botan's tonic working.

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:24.760
What if something else happens to you?

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:37.950
Is that...

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.170
A bear?

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:42.870
He's not very cute.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.760
What's a bear doing here?

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:53.450
Botan! Are you okay?

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.560
Hey, everyone!

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:59.310
Thanks for waiting.

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:03.350
I see you found Hanakoizumi-san. That's great.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.670
Y-Yeah, thanks, but—

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:09.100
Yeah, I'm a pretty good swimmer, right?

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:11.150
Timothy, behind you.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.270
Splash! Or so you thought, but look!

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:16.160
I can tread water, too! Amazing, huh?

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.400
Just look behind you!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.870
Okay, I'll dog paddle next.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.830
Seriously, look behind you!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:28.540
What? Don't scare me like that.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:34.750
Hey, is that a—

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:40.680
Like a salmon!

00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:42.830
Timo-Timothy!

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:53.310
D-Do you have anything to keep bears away?

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.740
Of course not!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:18.380
Get down!

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:43.930
Girls, are you all right?

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.030
Teacher!

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:48.300
I could hardly believe it when 
I heard over the radio

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:51.540
that a bear had escaped from the zoo.

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.790
Where did you get those guns?

00:19:55.790 --> 00:20:02.300
<b>Smile Smile</b>

00:19:56.110 --> 00:20:00.030
I need all kinds of licenses to protect students

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:02.300
as unfortunate as yourselves.

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:03.720
Although...

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:07.400
I never dreamed it'd be this serious.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:10.280
Oh, right.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:15.100
Here. It was near the creek.

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:17.460
Thanks!

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:19.630
Heave-ho.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.700
I'll take him back to the zoo while he's still

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.990
under the effects of the tranquilizer.

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:28.950
You girls head down the mountain
with the rest of the class.

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:34.940
A lot happened, but that was fun.

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:38.120
Really? I didn't have time to enjoy myself.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:42.630
I'm sorry for always being 
so useless in a pinch.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.940
I really am good for nothing.

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.010
What do you mean?

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:50.160
Your tonic and your umbrella saved us.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:51.980
Thanks, Botan-chan.

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:53.940
Girls...

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.220
More females?

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:02.180
But listening to birdsong 
while we walk isn't so bad.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:04.400
M-Maybe not.

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:12.540
I wouldn't want to fall or get lost again.

00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:15.100
You're right.

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:21.420
If I don't have a choice...

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.400
Here we go!

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:24.630
W-Wait!

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.510
Hurry, hurry!

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.420
You flew all the way to the ocean?

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:34.810
I swallowed a ton of sea water.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:37.770
Petting Zoo

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:37.770
Thank you so much.

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:39.980
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.730
Thank you again.

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:45.190
Maybe gold isn't my color after all...

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:53.080
Each of those girls has terrible luck,

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:57.000
but today's orienteering seems 
to have improved it some.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>June 28</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Visiting Hanako</b>

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:43.020
<b>Watch the next episode... or else!</b>
